# Enactment integrity violation: logic:EnactmentIntegrityViolation is a
# reasoner-materialized marker. The native enactment gate compiles every enactment-kernel
# logic:Constraint authored in this module into a violation-emitting forward rule — the
# law's antecedent joined with its NEGATED consequent — and drives them through the forward
# semi-naive chase over the reasoned graph, typing each condemned record with this class.
# This query does NOT recompute any law itself — it holds no FILTER NOT EXISTS structural
# check of its own, which is the whole point: restating a law here would be a second source
# of truth competing with the authored logic:Constraint. It only selects the already-derived
# marker and projects the record's own kernel type, so the surfaced finding names WHAT kind
# of enactment record was rejected and not merely that something was. Any returned row is a
# violation (design/LOGIC-ENACTMENT.md).
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>

SELECT ?subject ?recordType WHERE {
    ?subject a logic:EnactmentIntegrityViolation .
    OPTIONAL {
        ?subject a ?recordType .
        FILTER(?recordType != logic:EnactmentIntegrityViolation)
    }
}
ORDER BY ?subject ?recordType
